// Rule: [T1195.001] npm Cooldown - Npmrc File Event Coverage
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1195.001
// Classification: Validation query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceFileEvents
// Purpose: Endpoint telemetry validation for .npmrc activity before deploying privacy-preserving state snapshots.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceFileEvents for npmrc file event coverage using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: Defender recorded activity affecting .npmrc and the event can be assessed for path, action and creator completeness.
// A match does not prove: Cooldown removal, weak configuration, package compromise, secret access, malicious intent or T1195.001 execution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// npm cooldown state - endpoint file-event coverage
// Classification: Validation query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint -> DeviceFileEvents
//
// This query validates whether .npmrc activity is visible and whether the
// initiating-process and path fields are populated. It does NOT inspect file
// contents and therefore cannot prove that min-release-age was removed.
// Do not convert matches into alerts. Use the results to decide whether a
// privacy-preserving state snapshot is required for reliable posture monitoring.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FileName =~ ".npmrc"
| project Timestamp,
          DeviceId,
          DeviceName,
          ActionType,
          FileName,
          FolderPath,
          PreviousFileName,
          PreviousFolderPath,
          InitiatingProcessFileName,
          InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
          InitiatingProcessAccountUpn,
          InitiatingProcessAccountName,
          SHA1,
          ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
